  "description": "University-level single-variable analysis: functions, limits, continuity, differentiation, integration, sequences and series, with emphasis on rigorous reasoning and problem solving.",
  "prerequisites": [],
  "outcomes": [
    "Manipulate functions and inequalities confidently enough for university analysis.",
    "Evaluate and justify limits using both computational techniques and formal definitions.",
    "Use derivatives to analyze local and global behavior of functions.",
    "Understand the Riemann integral and the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus.",
    "Analyze basic sequences and series and communicate mathematical arguments clearly."
  ],
